      "title": "Pfizer Q2 results: Net profit rises 65.7% to ₹313 cr, income at ₹774 cr",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/pfizer-q2-results-net-profit-rises-65-7-to-313-cr-income-at-774-cr-126110301068_1.html",
      "description": "Drugmaker Pfizer Ltd on Tuesday reported a 65.72 per cent increase in net profit to Rs 313.25 crore in the September quarter, driven by gains from exceptional items.\nThe company had posted a profit of Rs 189 crore in the corresponding period of the previous fiscal year, Pfizer said in a regulatory filing.\nPfizer has accounted for exceptional gains of Rs 132.06 crore in the September quarter from its parent entity Pfizer Inc USA following the sale of Minipress XL. Consequent to the decision, Pfizer Ltd discontinued the manufacture of Minipress XL from September 7, 2026, according to the filing.\nIts profit before tax and exceptional items stood at Rs 290.77 crore during the quarter under review, up 13.86 per cent year-on-year. It was at Rs 255.37 crore in the corresponding quarter of the previous fiscal year.\nIts total income rose to Rs 774.19 crore during the quarter under review from Rs 684.19 crore in the year-ago period.\nPfizer reported an increase in total expenses to Rs 483.2",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-03T10:27:09"
    },
    {
      "title": "Zydus Wellness Q2 results: Net profit at ₹5.1 cr, revenue up at  ₹1,126 cr",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/zydus-wellness-q2-results-net-profit-at-5-1-cr-revenue-up-at-1-126-cr-126110300987_1.html",
      "description": "Zydus Wellness on Tuesday reported a consolidated net profit of Rs 5.1 crore in the September quarter due to higher revenues.\nThe company posted a net loss of Rs 52.8 crore in the corresponding period of the previous fiscal year, the company said in a regulatory filing.\nIts revenue from operations rose sharply to Rs 1,126.6 crore in the quarter under review, up from Rs 650.5 crore in the year-ago period, it added.\nTotal expenses increased to Rs 1,125.4 crore in the July-September period from Rs 668.3 crore a year earlier.\nZydus Wellness shares were trading 0.63 per cent higher at Rs 486.25 apiece on the BSE.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-03T10:04:59"
    }
